  "id": "COMPOUND:9138 - PROTEIN:1379",
  "verbalization": "Calcium gluconate is implicated in the regulation of G-protein coupled estrogen receptor 1 (GPER1) through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that calcium gluconate acts as a target for several compounds that modulate GPER1, including [(2-AMINO-ALPHA-METHOXYIMINO-4-THIAZOLYLACETYL)AMINO]METHYLBORONIC ACID, Linderagalactone E, and N-[(3-hydroxy-4-methoxyphenyl)methyl]-7-methyloctanamide. These compounds are all known to interact with GPER1, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the receptor. The presence of multiple targets for calcium gluconate suggests a broader role in the regulation of GPER1, possibly through the modulation of intracellular calcium levels or other signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between calcium gluconate and GPER1, emphasizing the need for further mechanistic investigation to fully understand the biological relevance of this interaction.",
